@page "/"
@using System.Collections
@using EwFrameworkAnalysis.Common.Models

<PageTitle>E-W Framework Analysis Tool</PageTitle>

<div class="min-h-screen bg-base-100">

    <section class="relative pt-16* items-center flex h-screen max-h-[860px]">
        <div class="container mx-auto items-center flex flex-wrap justify-center">
            <div class="w-full md:w-8/12 lg:w-6/12 xl:w-6/12 px-4">
                <div class="pt-32* sm:pt-0">
                    <h2 class="font-semibold text-4xl text-secondary pb-4">
                        What is the EW Framework?
                    </h2>
                    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed font-semibold text-secondary/80">
                        The <a href="https://educationtoworkforce.org/" class="link link-hover font-bold hover:text-primary/80">Education-to-Workforce Indicator Framework</a>
                        (or E-W Framework) is an extensive framework developed with input from leading experts from over 20 national and community organizations.
                        It highlights key connections needed between systems to support students as they progress from early education through their career.
                        <span class="font-bold">The E-W Framework includes:</span>
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        @* <img class="absolute top-0 b-auto right-0 pt-16 sm:w-6/12 -mt-48 sm:mt-0 w-10/12 max-h-860px"
            src="https://demos.creative-tim.com/notus-react/static/media/pattern_react.01996482.png" alt="..." style=""> *@
    </section>

    <section class="mt-48 md:mt-40 pb-40 relative bg-gray-100/60">
        <div class="-mt-20 top-0 bottom-auto left-0 right-0 w-full absolute h-20"
             style="transform: translateZ(0px)">
            <svg class="absolute bottom-0 overflow-hidden"
                 xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                 preserveAspectRatio="none"
                 version="1.1"
                 viewBox="0 0 2560 100"
                 x="0"
                 y="0">
                <polygon class="text-gray-100/60 fill-current"
                         points="2560 0 2560 100 0 100"></polygon>
            </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="container mx-auto">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center">
                <div class="w-10/12 md:w-6/12 lg:w-4/12 px-12 md:px-4 mr-auto ml-auto -mt-32*">
                    <div class="relative flex flex-col min-w-0 break-words bg-white* w-full mb-6 shadow-lg rounded-lg bg-secondary">
                        <img alt="..."
                             src="data:image/png;base64,"
                             class="w-full align-middle rounded-t-lg bg-white p-5 pb-8" />


                        <blockquote class="relative p-8 mb-4">
                            <svg preserveAspectRatio="none"
                                 xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                                 viewBox="0 0 583 95"
                                 class="absolute left-0 w-full block h-[95px] -top-[94px]">
                                <polygon points="-30,95 583,95 583,65"
                                         class="text-lightBlue-500 fill-current"></polygon>
                            </svg>
                            <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">
                                The E-W Framework includes:
                            </h4>
                            <p class="hidden text-md font-light mt-2 text-white">...</p>
                        </blockquote>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="w-full md:w-6/12 px-4">
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap">
                        <div class="w-full md:w-6/12 px-4">
                            <div class="relative flex flex-col mt-4">
                                <div class="px-4 py-5 flex-auto">
                                    <div class="text-secondary-500 p-3 text-center inline-flex items-center justify-center w-12 h-12 mb-5 shadow-lg rounded-full bg-white">
                                        <i class="fas fa-sitemap"></i>
                                    </div>
                                    <h6 class="text-xl mb-1 font-semibold">Essential questions</h6>
                                    <p class="mb-4 text-secondary-500">
                                        Twenty questions essential for E-W data systems to answer about how students are
                                        progressing from early education through career—and using the answers to guide action.
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="relative flex flex-col min-w-0">
                                <div class="px-4 py-5 flex-auto">
                                    <div class="text-secondary-500 p-3 text-center inline-flex items-center justify-center w-12 h-12 mb-5 shadow-lg rounded-full bg-white">
                                        <i class="fas fa-drafting-compass"></i>
                                    </div>
                                    <h6 class="text-xl mb-1 font-semibold">
                                        Indicators
                                    </h6>
                                    <p class="mb-4 text-secondary-500">
                                        Student outcomes and milestones and related system conditions
                                        associated with economic mobility and security, plus guidance
                                        on how to measure them (Metrics).
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="w-full md:w-6/12 px-4">
                            <div class="relative flex flex-col min-w-0 mt-4">
                                <div class="px-4 py-5 flex-auto">
                                    <div class="text-secondary-500 p-3 text-center inline-flex items-center justify-center w-12 h-12 mb-5 shadow-lg rounded-full bg-white">
                                        <i class="fas fa-newspaper"></i>
                                    </div>
                                    <h6 class="text-xl mb-1 font-semibold">Disaggregates</h6>
                                    <p class="mb-4 text-secondary-500">
                                        Characteristics that E-W systems should use to break down
                                        data, plus guidance on how to collect them.
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="relative flex flex-col min-w-0">
                                <div class="px-4 py-5 flex-auto">
                                    <div class="text-secondary-500 p-3 text-center inline-flex items-center justify-center w-12 h-12 mb-5 shadow-lg rounded-full bg-white">
                                        <i class="fas fa-file-alt"></i>
                                    </div>
                                    <h6 class="text-xl mb-1 font-semibold">Evidence-Based Practices</h6>
                                    <p class="mb-4 text-secondary">
                                        The framework is centered around equity-based
                                        principles and also provides evidence based practices.
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="relative items-center flex h-screen max-h-[460px] bg-gray-100/60">
        <div class="container mx-auto items-center flex flex-wrap justify-center">
            <div class="w-full md:w-8/12 lg:w-6/12 xl:w-6/12 px-4 ">
                <div class="pt-32* sm:pt-0">
                    <h2 class="font-semibold text-4xl text-secondary pb-4">
                        What does the E-W Analysis Tool do?
                    </h2>
                    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed font-semibold text-secondary/80">
                        This Analysis Tool was developed by Double Line to build upon the rich information in the
                        E-W Framework and enable you to understand which indicators your data systems are prepared for.
                        It then calculates how well your data satisfies the recommended metrics for each Indicator,
                        giving you a visual representation of your system's readiness by Indicator and by Essential Question.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Features Section -->
    <section class="py-12 bg-gray-100/60">
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
            <div class="card">
                <div class="card-body text-center">
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-white bg-gray-400 rounded-lg py-18 mb-2">Data Input Illustration</h3>
                    <p class="font-semibold">Input Your Data Inventory</p>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                        Provide details about your current data sources and elements through manual or automated methods.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <div class="card-body text-center">
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-white bg-gray-400 rounded-lg py-18 mb-2">Readiness Scores Chart</h3>
                    <p class="font-semibold">View Readiness Scores</p>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                        See instant feedback and visualize how well your data currently supports the E-W Framework’s indicators.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <div class="card-body text-center">
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-white bg-gray-400 rounded-lg py-18 mb-2">Roadmap Planning</h3>
                    <p class="font-semibold">Plan your roadmap</p>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                        Use the insights to understand gaps and prioritize efforts.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="relative items-center flex min-h-screen max-h-[1460px] bg-gray-100/60">
        <div class="container mx-auto items-center flex flex-wrap justify-center">
            <div class="w-full lg:w-8/12 xl:w-8/12 px-4 xl:px-24">
                <div class="pt-32* sm:pt-0 ">
                    <h2 class="font-semibold text-3xl text-secondary font-bold  mb-10">
                        Input your Data Inventory
                    </h2>

                    <div class="join join-vertical">
                        <!-- Step 1 -->
                        <div class="collapse collapse-arrow join-item">
                            <input type="checkbox" />
                            <div class="collapse-title text-lg font-semibold">
                                Navigate to the Dashboard
                            </div>
                            <div class="collapse-content">
                                <p>Create an E-W data readiness inventory directly from the dashboard.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Step 2 -->
                        <div class="collapse collapse-arrow join-item">
                            <input type="checkbox" />
                            <div class="collapse-title text-lg font-semibold">
                                Select and automatically interrogate an Ed-Fi ODS
                            </div>
                            <div class="collapse-content">
                                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
                                    <li>The E-W Analysis Tool can securely interrogate an Ed-Fi ODS through an API connection.</li>
                                    <li>Select <strong>Ed-Fi ODS</strong> as a Data Source.</li>
                                    <li>Input the appropriate connection details for your ODS.</li>
                                    <li>Click <strong>“Interrogate Data”</strong> to check data availability.</li>
                                    <li>View record counts and updated readiness results in Quick View.</li>
                                    <li>Provide extra info or manual scoring in the Details view.</li>
                                    <li>Supports multiple historical versions of this data source.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Step 3 -->
                        <div class="collapse collapse-arrow join-item">
                            <input type="checkbox" />
                            <div class="collapse-title text-lg font-semibold">
                                Select and automatically interrogate a CEDS Data Warehouse
                            </div>
                            <div class="collapse-content">
                                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
                                    <li>Download the CEDS DW SQL Interrogation Scripts.</li>
                                    <li>Run the scripts in your environment to interrogate CEDS DW tables.</li>
                                    <li>Scripts generate a Results File you can save to your computer.</li>
                                    <li>Upload the Results File into the E-W Analysis Tool.</li>
                                    <li>View record counts and readiness results in Quick View.</li>
                                    <li>Supports multiple historical versions of this data source.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Step 4 -->
                        <div class="collapse collapse-arrow join-item">
                            <input type="checkbox" />
                            <div class="collapse-title text-lg font-semibold">
                                Create Data Sources for manual input
                            </div>
                            <div class="collapse-content">
                                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
                                    <li>Create additional Data Sources for repositories not automatically interrogated.</li>
                                    <li>Input descriptions (e.g., Student Assessments, Postsecondary Statistics).</li>
                                    <li>Navigate to each data element to provide scoring and notes.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Step 5 -->
                        <div class="collapse collapse-arrow join-item">
                            <input type="checkbox" />
                            <div class="collapse-title text-lg font-semibold">
                                Download your results
                            </div>
                            <div class="collapse-content">
                                <p>Choose <strong>Save My Work</strong> to download your inventory results anytime.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Step 6 -->
                        <div class="collapse collapse-arrow join-item">
                            <input type="checkbox" />
                            <div class="collapse-title text-lg font-semibold">
                                Upload previous results
                            </div>
                            <div class="collapse-content">
                                <p>Choose <strong>Upload My Work</strong> to re-use previously saved results.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Step 7 -->
                        <div class="collapse collapse-arrow join-item">
                            <input type="checkbox" />
                            <div class="collapse-title text-lg font-semibold">
                                Configure which Data Sources to analyze
                            </div>
                            <div class="collapse-content">
                                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
                                    <li>Mark Data Sources you want to analyze as <strong>Active</strong>.</li>
                                    <li>Select <strong>Run Analysis</strong> to generate reports.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Step 8 -->
                        <div class="collapse collapse-arrow join-item">
                            <input type="checkbox" />
                            <div class="collapse-title text-lg font-semibold">
                                View quick results on the Dashboard
                            </div>
                            <div class="collapse-content">
                                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
                                    <li>Summary results for multiple measures appear on the Dashboard.</li>
                                    <li>Quick view of essential questions is also available.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ Section-->
    <section class="relative items-center flex">
        <div class="container mx-auto items-center flex flex-wrap justify-center ">
            <div class="w-full xl:w-8/12 *px-4 ">
                <div class="pt-32 sm:pt-24">
                    <h2 class="font-semibold text-4xl pb-12">
                        Frequently Asked Questions
                    </h2>

                    @foreach (var faq in faqs)
                    {
                        <div class="collapse collapse-arrow border-b rounded-none py-8 ">
                            <input type="checkbox" name="faq-list" />
                            <div class="collapse-title font-semibold text-2xl hover:cursor-pointer hover:underline">@faq.Question</div>
                            <div class="collapse-content ">@((MarkupString)faq.Answer)</div>
                        </div>
                    }
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Call to Action -->
    <section class="py-16 text-center h-screen max-h-[800px]">
        <div class="container mx-auto items-center flex flex-wrap justify-center ">
            <div class="w-full xl:w-8/12 ">
                <div class="pt-32 sm:pt-24">

                    <h2 class="font-semibold text-4xl pb-12">Ready to Get Started?</h2>
                    <p class="mb-6 font-semibold text-gray-600">
                        Begin your data readiness assessment today with the E-W Framework Analysis Tool.
                    </p>
                    <button class="btn btn-secondary">Start Analysis</button>

                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>


@code {
    private List<FAQItem> faqs = new()
    {
        new FAQItem
        {
            Question = "How do I automatically interrogate my Ed-Fi ODS?",
            Answer = @"
                <ul class=""list -mx-4"">
                    <li class=""list-row""><p>Select Ed-Fi ODS as a Data Source.</p></li>
                    <li class=""list-row""><p>Input the appropriate connection details for your ODS.</p></li>
                    <li class=""list-row""><p>“Interrogate Data” to have the E-W Analysis Tool connect to and interrogate your ODS for E-W data availability.</p></li>
                    <li class=""list-row""><p>Upon successful completion of the interrogation, you will see statistics such as the count of records found, and the impact of your updated data readiness results will immediately display in the Quick View.</p></li>
                    <li class=""list-row""><p>You can provide additional information about each data element by clicking into the Details and manually scoring each data element and providing additional notes.</p></li>
                    <li class=""list-row""><p>Multiple historical versions of this data source can be supported.</p></li>
                </ul>
            "},
        new FAQItem {
            Question = "Is the automatic interrogation of my Ed-Fi ODS safe and secure?",
            Answer = @"
                <p>The interaction with the API will be between the user’s browser and their API, and the E-W Analysis Tool website server will never receive
                the entered credentials nor will it be in the middle of the API traffic. The E-W Analysis Tool website server will only receive the results
                metadata, to include the fields for which data exists and some profiling of the nature of that data.</p>
            " },
        new FAQItem {
            Question = "What if I have a non-standard implementation of an Ed-Fi ODS?",
            Answer = @"
                <p>Any modifications made to the standard implementation of an Ed-Fi ODS may disrupt the automated interrogation of the API call.</p>
            " },
        new FAQItem {
            Question = "What if my Ed-Fi ODS uses a different version of Ed-Fi than version 5 of the data standard and version 7 of the API?",
            Answer = @"
                <ul class=""list -mx-4"">
                    <li class=""list-row""><p>The tool is developed and tested against Ed-Fi ODS API version 7.3 (Data Standard v5). Because many of the Ed-Fi API specifications overlap across versions, some checks may still work with other versions, but compatibility is not guaranteed.</p></li>
                    <li class=""list-row""><p>If a check produces an inaccurate or missing result due to version differences, you can override the result within the tool or provide the needed information as a Custom data source. These options help ensure the analysis remains accurate even if your ODS is running a different Ed-Fi version.</p></li>
                </ul>
            " },
        new FAQItem {
            Question = "How do I automatically interrogate my CEDS Data Warehouse?",
            Answer = @"
                <ul class=""list -mx-4"">
                    <li class=""list-row""><p> To interrogate a CEDS Data Warehouse, download the CEDS DW SQL Interrogation Scripts.</p></li>
                    <li class=""list-row""><p> Run the SQL Interrogation Scripts in your own environment. </p></li>
                    <li class=""list-row""><p> The Scripts are designed to interrogate the appropriate standard CEDS DW tables for the data elements that are necessary to create E-W Indicators to answer E-W Essential Questions. </p></li>
                    <li class=""list-row""><p> Once the Scripts complete, they will generate a Results File that can be saved to your computer. </p></li>
                    <li class=""list-row""><p> Upload the Results File to the E-W Analysis Tool. </p></li>
                    <li class=""list-row""><p> Upon successful upload of the Results File, you will see statistics such as the count of records found, and the impact of your updated data readiness results will immediately display in the Quick View. </p></li>
                    <li class=""list-row""><p> Multiple historical versions of this data source can be supported. </p></li>
                </ul>
            " },
        new FAQItem {
            Question = "Is the automatic interrogation of my CEDS Data Warehouse safe and secure?",
            Answer = @"
                <ul class=""list -mx-4"">
                    <li class=""list-row""><p> The E-W Analysis Tool provides SQL scripts for the user to execute locally.  Results can be exported to a plaintext file that can be reviewed for sensitive data before uploading to the publicly hosted application. This method maintains user control, aligns with security best practices, and accommodates air-gapped systems isolated from the public Internet. </p></li>
                    <li class=""list-row""><p> By decoupling data profiling from the hosted application, the tool ensures compliance with security and accessibility standards without compromising functionality or ease of use. </p></li>
                </ul>
            " },
        new FAQItem {
            Question = "What if my CEDS Data Warehouse is different from Version 11?",
            Answer = @"
                <p>[Answer pending]</p>
            " },
        new FAQItem {
            Question = "What data does the E-W Analysis Tool collect and store?",
            Answer = @"
                <ul class=""list -mx-4"">
                    <li class=""list-row""><p> Results of a user’s browser session are only stored for the duration of the session. </p></li>
                    <li class=""list-row""><p> The E-W Analysis Tool website server will only receive results metadata from automated data system interrogations, to include the fields for which data exists and some profiling of the nature of that data. </p></li>
                    <li class=""list-row""><p> User input of data sources is limited to similar metadata descriptions, such as additional scoring criteria and data source notes. </p></li>
                    <li class=""list-row""><p> The E-W Analysis Tool does not have the capacity to store any other types of data such as sensitive information. </p></li>
                    <li class=""list-row""><p> Data inventory results can be saved to a file on the user’s computer, and can be subsequently re-uploaded. </p></li>
                </ul>
            " },
        new FAQItem {
            Question = "How does your Data Readiness scoring work?",
            Answer = @"
                <ul class=""list -mx-4"">
                    <li class=""list-row""><p> The automated data interrogation process (i.e., Ed-Fi ODS API and CEDS DW SQL queries) queries the respective databases about the presence of particular data in the standard tables that have been mapped to E-W Framework Indicators and Metrics.  In addition to Counts of records, the tool looks at other characteristics that may indicate quality of data, such as checking for non-Numeric values where the data element is of Numeric type. </p></li>
                    <li class=""list-row""><p> The manual data input process allows the user to add additional data sources and to modify the results of automated data interrogations.  Part of the input process enables the user to score each data element for Availability (does the data exist), Accessibility (is the data accessible to the parties that need it), and Quality (is the data of high quality). </p></li>
                    <li class=""list-row""><p> The E-W Analysis Tool takes the results of the automated data interrogation and manual inputs and applies a scoring rubric to each data element.  Each data element then rolls up into one or more Indicators as a necessary component of readiness, and each Indicator then rolls up to one or more Essential Question as a necessary component of readiness. </p></li>
                </ul>
            " },
        new FAQItem {
            Question = "How can I use the results I generate?",
            Answer = @"
                <ul class=""list -mx-4"">
                    <li class=""list-row""><p> The E-W Framework is thorough and presents an incredibly rich set of findings. However, it is voluminous and may be overwhelming to many potential users who could benefit greatly from its content. Additionally, each user of the E-W Framework must make their own effort to bridge its research-backed components to the practical realities of the availability, location, and quality of their data. </p></li>
                    <li class=""list-row"">
                        <div>
                            <p> States do not start their P20W+ infrastructure from zero. At the time they decide to move toward a P20W+, states have existing data systems at varied levels of data maturity that overlap in whole or in part with the 4 sectors of the E-W Framework. Similarly, Local Education Agencies (LEAs) also have existing systems in place when exploring systems integration and expansion of their P12+ infrastructure . When introduced to the E-W Framework, we anticipate States, LEAs, and their supporting vendors will have questions such as: </p>
                            <p class=""px-6 py-4"">	What research questions do I need to answer to demonstrate the value of a P20W system to the state?</p>
                            <p class=""px-6 py-4"">	What data elements are already collected statewide that can answer those questions (and do I have access to them)?</p>
                            <p class=""px-6 py-4"">	How should I prioritize essential questions and indicators to start with?</p>
                            <p class=""px-6 py-4"">	What can I do to get more data into the system in the future to answer the essential questions I’m most interested in?</p>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                    <li class=""list-row""><p> The E-W Analysis Tool is a free and simple way to analyze an end-user’s (e.g., state education agency, local education agency) own data preparedness and guide their own internal discussions around which Essential Questions they should be prioritizing. This will lead to prioritizing their own data work to build infrastructure to answer those questions, and enabling these organizations to build a roadmap for short-term goals to implement early and for longer-term goals to start discussions around. </p></li>
                </ul>
            " }
    };
}
